        "id": "f00abd1607c200836333494aa39da91bdc59e5c6",
        "message": "[Backport 5.x] feat: add routerOptions.compile to use find-my-way compiler mode (#7116)\n\nProposal:\n\nManual backport of #7096 to `5.x`: the automated backport failed with\nconflicts, see\nhttps://github.com/fastify/fastify/pull/7096#issuecomment-6155131364.\n\nCherry-pick of fcba984c0a41d7cfacff5234e0594d3b561cb804 with these\nconflict resolutions:\n\n- `build/build-validation.js` / `lib/config-validator.js`: `main` moved\n`allowUnsafeRegex`, `caseSensitive` and `constraints` into\n`routerOptions`, which is not the case on 5.x. Only `compile: false` is\nadded, then the validator was regenerated with `npm run\nbuild:validation`.\n- `fastify.d.ts`: only `compile?: boolean` is added to\n`FastifyRouterOptions`, without the `constraints` rework from v6.\n- `fastify.js`: kept `VERSION = '5.12.7'`.\n- `test/internals/initial-config.test.js`: kept the 5.x snapshot (no\n`routerOptions` in the defaults).\n- `lib/route.js`: added the `defaultInitOptions` import from\n`./initial-config-validation.js`, which `main` already had and the new\n`routerOptions.compile ??=` line needs.\n- `test/router-compile.test.js`: on 5.x `initialConfig.routerOptions` is\nonly exposed when the user passes it, so the \"defaults to false\" test\nasserts `undefined` instead of `.compile === false`. Everything else is\nunchanged.\n\nNote:\n\n`.npmrc` also carries over the `min-release-age-exclude[]=find-my-way`\nentry, needed until `find-my-way@9.10.0` is older than 7 days\n(2026-10-17).\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Tony133 <a.tripodi133@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-14T21:19:51Z",
